prior to the announced public hearing is September12,2022.The earliest confirmation of
deliverywas dated September12,2022.
The application complies with this review criterion.
CONFORMANCE WITH APPLICABLE PLANS:
The project is located in an area covered by the following plans:
·Plan Cheyenne
Policies within Plan Cheyenne encourage responsible growth.As this annexation is on the edge of the
community, any development action needs to take into careful consideration how to extend
infrastructure.
The Future Land Use Map of Plan Cheyenne, as updated by Connect 2045, anticipates this area of the
community to develop with urban residential and some commercial uses.Theseareas areexpected to
develop withfull access to urban services-such areas are best servedby being within City limits.An
amendment to Plan Cheyenne is proposed which would change the designation of the subject property
to Mixed-use Employment.This proposed use category is also best served by being within City limits.
Thearea is within the Urban Service Boundary, whichmeans that nomatter the specific development
services.
STAFF REVIEW:
Through thereview process, the following comments were received:
Technical corrections to the annexation map
CONCLUSION:
Staffis satisfied that the application meets the review criteria and therefore recommends approval of
the annexation.
The proposed annexation is a natural extension of the City, is contiguous to the current City limits, and
most services typically available tourban areas are available tobe extended to this property.
STAFF RECOMMENDATION:
Staff recommends approval of the annexation of the property.
ATTACHMENTS:
1.Current Zoning Map
2.Future Land Use Map
3.Submitted Application
4.Applicant-submitted annexation map
